{"timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:18:29.592Z","ordinal":402,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a19ecc-82f0-7492-9f12-a328e4f8c843","turn_id":"01a1a459-abe7-7952-8326-cf2cf0e2cc59","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_080347deb607e55e016aea95f252d8819bb611c34ebe2cfda6","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’d keep **`sun push` and add `sun pull`** as explicit commands:\n\n- `sun push`: publish recorded Sun history without pushing Git commits.\n- `sun pull`: fetch and join remote Sun history, preserving the local snapshot.\n- `git push` / `git pull`: automatically invoke that same functionality through the integration.\n\nThat gives users a way to share Sun history when their Git commits haven’t changed, and works without shell integration. The automatic path should reuse these commands’ implementation.\n\n`sun pull` should clearly report that it joined history without applying remote file edits."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793758706276,"completed_at_ms":1793758709592}}
